@def MICRO_OS_PLUS_UTILS_LISTS_ENABLED
@brief Enable the µOS++ C++ Intrusive Lists library.

@details
The macro is intended to be defined by the user, 
typically in 
the library's own
`micro-os-plus/utils/lists-defines.h` configuration file or the 
project `micro-os-plus/project-config.h` configuration file.

When `MICRO_OS_PLUS_UTILS_LISTS_ENABLED` is defined, the C++ 
classes are compiled to their full implementations, declared
in @ref lists.h.

When it is not defined, no classes or functions are defined.